    "summary": "Wired the objective ledger into MatchRoom (apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts, new objectives.ts). A slice ledger is seeded from the room's private randomness. Its sources are 2 per island at the island's docks, and all are unlocked until the ruins are wired. Holding E while moored collects the island's first eligible source, or else claims a cached rubbing; release, cast-off, reservation or disconnect resets the hold, and starting one ends protection via protectionEndedBy. Duels: reserveDuel and reportDuelResult are called, and 'settled' goes to the encounter rules only once the ledger settles (choose-theft message, protocol v6, zod-validated, winner only; the default applies at the deadline). The world tick drives section 12: disconnectPlayer at the drop, a 10 s duel absence counted in ticks, expireReservation at the deadline into a cache at the rules' respawn dock, and every other leave (including Colyseus' 70 s outer bound) is a quitPlayer into a cache at the nearest dock by sea. checkLedger plus a room invariant (no ship without a ledger player and vice versa) run every tick in development and tests; production turns them off. Hidden info: gold, rubbings, holds and theft options are in the player's own status only; island and cache types only while moored there; contentless cache markers within sight; the grapple defenderId is blanked through a twin entry. Web: purse panel (gold, rubbings, settlement notice, theft choice on keys 1/2 or a click), HUD island/cache/hold progress/result lines, cache chests. Marker drawing moved to a Phaser-free markers.ts with a unit test. The match game was switched to Phaser.CANVAS after the measured tick p95 failed with AUTO (135 ms; 8.5/8.9 ms with canvas). Tests: new integration files rubbings/rubbingsExpiry/rubbingsOuterBound (one tuning per file, since there is one matchmaker per process); seaDuel updates (moving ship stops on reservation, ready-timeout cancel at 200 ticks, tick-counted absence); a real draw moving nothing in seaDuelHarness; web and server unit tests; the theft-loop Playwright scenario; sea-duel taps keys and asserts the tick p95. Integration budget: test-only overrides first (startGameServer matchTuning, duelReconnectSeconds), then fork parallelism (3 workers) with the harness files in a serial second group. Before: 201.65 s (old 55-test suite). Overrides only, serial, 73 tests: 263.64 s. Final: 117.17 s with the harness green. Checks actually run in this worktree: npm run typecheck (pass), npm run test:unit (900 pass), npm run test:integration (73 pass, 117.17 s), npm run build (pass, smoke test extended), and the full Playwright suite with a JSON report: 8/8 pass, check-report ok for all 8 scenarios. Docs updated: architecture.md, duel.md, encounters.md, objectives.md and README.md.",
